## Rework verification, 2026-10-28 23:38 Europe/Zurich (F1 masthead, F2 undo mid-stroke)
- harness: the same raw-CDP driver, fresh Chrome profile, 1440 × 900; 30 assertions, all passed, no console error or page exception
### Masthead after applyLocale (F1)
- EN: lastChange "Last change: P0-43 — Live demo: pen tool and ink colours over the whole board", lastChangeTime "2026-10-28 23:07 (Europe/Zurich)", tasks "Tasks: P0-19, …, P0-42, P0-43, P1-07"
- the rendered EN lastChange, time and task list equal the index.html fallback text byte for byte after the locale fetch (no P0-42 title, no 22:07)
- DE: lastChange "Letzte Änderung: P0-43 — Live-Demo: Stift und Tintenfarben über das ganze Board", lastChangeTime "2026-10-28 23:07 (Europe/Zurich)", tasks "Aufgaben: P0-19, …, P0-42, P0-43, P1-07"
- the rendered DE strings equal locales/de.json (same key set as en.json, no "ß", du-form); EN and DE agree on P0-43, 23:07 and the task list ending P0-42, P0-43, P1-07
### Undo mid-stroke (F2 repro)
- stroke 1 in tone-a committed: ink paths=1
- stroke 2 started with the pointer still down (8 moves): ink paths=2
- Cmd/Ctrl+Z mid-stroke: ink paths=0, hint "Undo: Draw" — the live stroke and stroke 1 are gone
- releasing the pointer after the cancelled stroke: ink paths=0, hint unchanged "Undo: Draw"; no "Undo: Move" step was recorded and nothing cleared the redo stack
- second Cmd/Ctrl+Z after the release: ink paths=0 — there is no spurious history entry to consume
- Shift+Cmd/Ctrl+Z: ink paths=1, hint "Redo: Draw", tones ["tone-a"] — redo restores the real previous step
- normal undo/redo without a live stroke: 1 → 0 → 1 path, hints "Undo: Draw" / "Redo: Draw"
- regression after leaving the pen: dragging note A records "Undo: Move", undo restores the position and keeps the ink (press snapshot path intact)

## Final verification, 2026-10-28 23:47 Europe/Zurich (F4 multi-pointer guard, F5 colour survival)
- harness: the same raw-CDP driver, fresh Chrome profile, 1440 × 900, one loaded page for the colour sequence and fresh reloads for the pointer cases; no console error or page exception in any part.

### Colour survival across theme and language (F5, one session)
- start: theme=light, lang=en, pen off, default swatch tone-a, dot=oklch(0.455 0.065 165), ink paths=0
- pen selected; palette opened; swatch tone-d clicked: aria-pressed=["tone-d"], dot=oklch(0.45 0.08 255), status "Pen selected — Blue. Draw on the board; Escape ends the pen."
- two mouse strokes drawn: ink paths=2, tones=["tone-d","tone-d"], stroke colour oklch(0.45 0.08 255) for both, status "Stroke drawn in Blue."
- Cmd/Ctrl+Z: ink paths=1, hint "Undo: Draw"; Shift+Cmd/Ctrl+Z: ink paths=2, hint "Redo: Draw", tones still ["tone-d","tone-d"]
- theme light → dark: theme=dark, ink paths=2, tones unchanged, dot=rgb(143, 176, 220), stroke colour rgb(143, 176, 220), status unchanged
- language EN → DE: lang=de, ink paths=2, tones unchanged, dot=rgb(143, 176, 220) (same dark tone-d); the locale switch clears the status line by design, then re-selecting the pen announces "Stift ausgewählt — Blau. Zeichne auf der Leinwand; Escape beendet den Stift."
- theme dark → light: theme=light, ink paths=2, tones unchanged, dot=oklch(0.45 0.08 255) (light tone-d), stroke colour oklch(0.45 0.08 255), status unchanged
- language DE → EN: lang=en, ink paths=2, tones unchanged, dot=oklch(0.45 0.08 255); re-selecting the pen announces "Pen selected — Blue. Draw on the board; Escape ends the pen."
- result: the same tone-d token is kept through light → dark → DE → light → EN; only the resolved value follows the theme (oklch in light, rgb(143, 176, 220) in dark), in both directions, and both strokes survive every switch.

### Multi-pointer guard (F4)
- non-primary pointer: fresh load, pen selected, no live stroke; a synthetic pointerdown with isPrimary=false, pointerId 77, pointerType=touch on the surface left ink paths=0, event.defaultPrevented=false (the guard returns before preventDefault) and started no stroke.
- real two-finger touch: fresh load, pen selected, `Emulation.setTouchEmulationEnabled` with maxTouchPoints=5, then one `Input.dispatchTouchEvent` touchStart with two points (primary at surface +400/+220, non-primary at surface +620/+300).
- after touchStart: exactly one live path, d="M 399.0 171.0" — the second, non-primary pointer neither started nor replaced a stroke (without the guard, the first partial path would have been orphaned in the SVG and the second would have become the live path, i.e. two `path` elements).
- after touchMove moving both fingers (primary +40/+30, second +60/+40): the same path reads d="M 399.0 171.0 L 439.0 201.0" — only the primary pointer's sample was appended; the second finger's movement was not drawn.
- after touchEnd: ink paths=1, tones=["tone-a"], status "Stroke drawn in Sage.", pen still active.
- Cmd/Ctrl+Z: ink paths=0, hint "Undo: Draw"; Shift+Cmd/Ctrl+Z: ink paths=1, tone-a, hint "Redo: Draw" — the touch stroke is exactly one history step.
- normal mouse pen and its undo/redo are unaffected: the two mouse strokes and their undo/redo in the colour sequence above passed with the guard in place.

